  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Conceptualizing the AI Docent**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the core functionalities for the React application. Key features will include an AI-powered guide for European pilgrims, specializing in both historical and theological insights. I\'m exploring the integration of React, Vite, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS to ensure a robust and visually appealing user experience, focusing on seamless information delivery.\n\n\n**Refining the Application Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the application\'s core workflow. The key will be the ability for users to input Latin, Italian, or Spanish inscriptions and receive a deep, faith-based analysis. I\'m prioritizing the user experience, allowing input via typing, pasting, image upload, or presets. I\'ve confirmed that Firebase isn\'t necessary, local storage for history is sufficient. A map feature to highlight famous inscriptions in Europe is also now on the table as a very helpful, but non-essential, feature.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the `gemini-api` skill file to learn the correct setup and patterns for using the `@google/genai` SDK in a secure server-side manner."
