    thinking: "**Analyzing Gemini API Usage**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of using the `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK. The goal is clear: to integrate the Gemini API seamlessly. I\'ve noted the import statement, and the instantiation of the `GoogleGenAI` class. This seems like a promising starting point for interaction with the model.\n\n\n**Establishing Server-Side Interaction**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on server-side implementation. No `server.ts` exists, but the `express` dependency suggests a full-stack approach is possible. I will prioritize creating server-side API routes (`/api/*`) for proxying requests, essential for secure API key management and to satisfy the project guidelines. I\'m noting the clear imperative to use a full-stack (server + client) architecture, which will be the basis of my next steps.\n\n\n"
