  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the interactive UI. My plan: allow pilgrims to input inscriptions via text or file upload. I\'ll include drag-and-drop functionality, and will incorporate support for local camera capture. Considering the UI constraints, I aim for a seamless, intuitive experience.\n\n\n**Refining the Preset Feature**\n\nI\'m developing the \"Curated Presets\" feature. Now, if a visitor clicks a preset, they can see a pre-populated analysis immediately or trigger the live API call using the server-side `/api/analyze` request, showcasing the Gemini integration. I\'ll cache the results in local state to improve response times for repeated presets. The preset analysis will use the real server integration.\n\n\n**Adding the History Feature**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a \"History Journal\" feature, allowing pilgrims to save and revisit analyzed inscriptions locally using `localStorage`. They\'ll be able to review, delete, and add personal notes to their entries, creating a travel journal of their faith. This will stay in line with the scope, allowing them to better manage their explorations. I\'ve also verified the Lucide icons import format and their availability. Finally, I\'m starting to build out `/src/App.tsx`, and I\'ll focus on designing an elegant stone-carving panel UI with a bento box layout.\n\n\n**Designing the Input Panel**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the left column, the input panel. I\'m building a form for text input and image upload via a dropzone. I\'m also adding six preset inscription options, arranged in a masonry or slider format, each with location badges (\"\353\260\224\355\213\260\354\271\270\", \"\355\224\274\353\240\214\354\262\264\", etc.). A \"\353\266\204\354\204\235 \354\213\234\354\236\221\" (Begin Divine Analysis) button with an animated icon will trigger the process.\n\n\n**Implementing the Analysis Steps**\n\nI\'m now implementing the analysis steps, creating historical-themed meditation steps like \"\353\254\270\355\227\214 \353\214\200\354\241\260 \354\244\221...\" and \"\353\235\274\355\213\264\354\226\264 \355\225\231\354\236\220 \354\230\201\352\260\220 \352\262\260\354\247\221 \354\244\221...\" to guide the user. The final display will be neatly organized according to the five specified rules: original text, biblical matching, Korean translation (with direct and interpretive versions), grammar/etymology tips, and spiritual guidance. I\'m focusing on crafting an elegant design, including features like copy-to-clipboard and save-to-history buttons for export.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/PresetGallery.tsx` to handle the grid layout of our beautiful curated historic pilgrim presets. This lets users explore the Vatican, Florence, and Santiago de Compostela monuments with an interactive tap."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 827935209
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
