  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Immediate Actions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how users expect immediate results when they upload a file, specifically with `handleFileChange` or `handleDrop`. This means I need to trigger `handleAnalyze` as soon as `imgData` is set up. I\'m exploring the React lifecycle to ensure this happens seamlessly.\n\n\n**Implementing Automatic Analysis**\n\nMy focus has shifted to implementing automatic analysis. I\'ve decided the most stable approach is to directly call `handleAnalyze` within `reader.onloadend`. This avoids state inconsistencies. I\'ll be modifying the code to trigger analysis immediately after setting the `selectedImage` state and clearing the error message. This auto-analysis happens the instant a file is selected or taken, which I think is very good.\n\n\n**Automating Text Input**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `purifiedText` from the AI analysis. The plan is to automatically populate the \"discovery phrase\" input field (`inputText`) with the corrected text returned from the AI response. Specifically, when `result.purifiedText` exists, I\'ll update the `inputText` state immediately. I have verified that this `purifiedText` corresponds to the \"1. Original text & correction purified\" section on the web interface.\n\n\n"
